{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/goruck-spy-ruck-womens-vest", "version_id": "b2b399ae8459a57c014a5f98177798eb25042a18d25351b54e818e7c99e34dee", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Relevant rucking-vest content with a hands-on fit report, but it rests on one reviewer's few weeks of personal wear with no durability result, and the review units and affiliate commissions come from GORUCK, a brand that is not a Mammoth sponsor but whose praise carries a commercial incentive. Under the Credibility and Commercial incentives sections, the single-source, self-reported fit impression is too thin to rely on yet, and it duplicates the vest-category coverage without a comparative or independent test.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/goruck-ruck-shuffle-basic-rucker", "version_id": "1ee84564c3fae6506fa8596ffdda0ca171a6d702feb3e3991d8d94de996e9bff", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Under the Relevance and Credibility sections the piece engages real evidence (two MTSU studies of the airborne shuffle and load-carriage biomechanics), but its central claim about the knee benefit of the shuffle versus jogging is unsupported by any cited study, and it promotes a GORUCK campaign with affiliate commissions and review units. The Unsupported claims section calls for deferral when the item rests mainly on significant claims lacking evidence, and its shuffle-training content is more a training-method topic than gear suitability for Mammoth.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/best-rucking-books-2026", "version_id": "f06c08c3ade5c2178960760c580c92bda32465f8847eac7abf3261e947992775", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section, books are not among the in-scope gear categories and the item is a sales-oriented book roundup with affiliate commissions and no hands-on gear evidence bearing on Mammoth conditions. It is an out-of-scope promotional guide that does not help a competitor decide what to carry.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/first-30-days-of-rucking", "version_id": "e7478e892d0b68e86e3590cf5a6aee352334952687a2aa6cc21c5af1eb937f84", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section this is a training plan for beginner loaded walking, not gear evaluation, and it is explicitly not event preparation, so it does not serve the gear-decision question. Its reliance on editorial starting points and an evidence base that is mostly military and not tested for civilian schedules also fails the Credibility standard for specific claims.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/how-heavy-should-your-ruck-be", "version_id": "9493cd846697b7ce4138fb6d9363ca50e8390becab392ba0cd1b2ad55ab62c63", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section this is a training-load calculator and progression guide rather than gear evaluation, and its central content (conservative 5-10 lb starting points and body-weight percentages) is editorial guidance that the source itself says is not a threshold. It does not offer gear performance evidence that helps a competitor decide what to carry.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/what-is-rucking-weighted-walking-explained", "version_id": "4e30a87b3843f861ad970752ef7c31a5e66c382cec6a22c681cbd6891698511f", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section this is an introductory explainer on what rucking is, with no evaluation of specific gear and no new evidence about equipment performance under Mammoth conditions. It duplicates general background and carries affiliate-linked gear mentions without substantive independent testing.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/injuries/rucking-knee-pain", "version_id": "efaf546f0140dab528ea219954dc01c47943dd1496c66a140ccf8cf559ce6ede", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section this is medical and injury-management content rather than gear evaluation, and it is outside the in-scope gear categories. Its gear mentions (a cushioned shoe and an insole) are promotional affiliate-adjacent asides with no independent test evidence about performance at Mammoth.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/injuries/rucking-shin-splints-prevention-early-signs-and-recovery-pro", "version_id": "c326a48b8e179a83b08b5738d25659335affea5b0b8b625a7a0189038beb4ced", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section this is medical injury content about medial tibial stress syndrome rather than gear evaluation, and it falls outside the in-scope gear categories. Its footwear and insole mentions are not supported by product-specific independent testing, so it does not help a competitor decide what to carry.", "piece_ids": []}
